{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the eyes of Leah were tender.</b> An expression of soft and good, meaning that she appeared beautiful, since her eyes were beautiful and she appeared soft, and she gave birth. But Rachel was more praiseworthy in her beauty, except that her eyes ached from weeping, because she saw that she would fall to the lot of Esau — since she was barren, Jacob would divorce her, and Esau would marry her."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:14.832155598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}